---
import { SmartLink } from "@repo/ui"
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Victor Fernandes"
  description="Read the privacy policy for Victor Fernandes' personal website and software engineering projects."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl p-8">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>Last updated:</strong> April 16, 2026 <br />&nbsp;
    </p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how information is collected, used, and protected when you visit
      <SmartLink href="https://victor-fernandes.com" showExternalIcon>victor-fernandes.com</SmartLink> (the "Website").
    </p>

    <p>
      If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or how your information is handled, please{" "}
      <SmartLink href="/contact/">contact</SmartLink>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">1. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy applies to information collected through this Website and related pages on the{" "}
      <code>victor-fernandes.com</code> domain. It does not apply to information collected offline or through third-party
      websites, services, or platforms that may be linked from this Website.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">2. Consent</h2>
    <p>
      By using this Website, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy. Where required by
      law, you also consent to the collection and use of information as described here.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">3. Information Collected</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-6 pb-0">3.1 Information you provide voluntarily</h3>
    <p>
      If you contact me through a form, email link, or other communication method, I may collect the information you
      choose to provide, such as:
    </p>
    <p>
      Name, email address, phone number (if provided), message content, attachments, and any other information you
      include in your communication.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 pb-0">3.2 Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      Like most websites, the Website and its hosting providers may automatically collect certain technical information
      when you visit, such as:
    </p>
    <p>
      IP address, browser type, device type, operating system, Internet Service Provider (ISP), referring/exit pages,
      date/time stamps, and general usage data (for example, pages viewed and clicks).
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 pb-0">3.3 Cookies and similar technologies</h3>
    <p>
      The Website may use cookies or similar technologies to improve functionality, remember preferences, and understand
      how visitors use the Website.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can usually control or disable cookies through your browser settings. Disabling cookies may affect some
      features of the Website, but the Website should generally remain usable.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">4. How Information Is Used</h2>
    <p>Information collected may be used for the following purposes:</p>
    <p>
      To operate and maintain the Website; to respond to messages and inquiries; to improve content, usability, and
      performance; to monitor usage and diagnose technical issues; to help prevent spam, abuse, and fraud; and to comply
      with legal obligations where applicable.
    </p>

    <p>
      This Website is a personal portfolio site. Information is <strong>not</strong> collected for unrelated marketing campaigns
      or sold as a business data product.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">5. Legal Bases for Processing (GDPR/UK GDPR, where applicable)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), the UK, or another region with similar laws, personal data
      may be processed on one or more of the following legal bases:
    </p>
    <p>
      Your consent; performance of a contract or pre-contractual steps (for example, responding to a project inquiry);
      legitimate interests (such as securing and improving the Website); and compliance with legal obligations.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">6. Log Files</h2>
    <p>
      The Website may use standard log files maintained by hosting providers and infrastructure services. These logs can
      include IP addresses, browser information, timestamps, referring/exit pages, and similar technical data. Log data
      is used for site administration, security, troubleshooting, and aggregate analytics.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">7. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      The Website may rely on third-party services (for example, hosting providers, CDN/security services, analytics
      providers, form/email delivery services, or embedded content providers). These third parties may process technical
      data as part of delivering their services.
    </p>

    <p>
      Examples (if used) may include hosting/platform services, analytics tools, spam protection, and embedded content
      (such as GitHub, LinkedIn, YouTube, or other social/media embeds).
    </p>

    <p>
      Each third-party service has its own privacy policy and data practices. Please review their policies for more
      information.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">8. Sharing of Information</h2>
    <p>Personal information is not sold. Information may be shared only when reasonably necessary, such as:</p>
    <p>
      With service providers that help operate the Website; to protect the rights, safety, and security of the Website
      or others; or when required by law, regulation, legal process, or government request.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">9. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Personal information is retained only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy,
      including responding to inquiries, maintaining records, resolving disputes, enforcing agreements, and meeting
      legal, tax, or security obligations.
    </p>

    <p>
      For example, contact form messages or emails may be retained for a reasonable period to continue conversations,
      maintain project history, or comply with legal obligations, after which they may be deleted or anonymized.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">10. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      Reasonable technical and organizational measures are used to protect personal information from unauthorized
      access, loss, misuse, or alteration. However, no method of transmission over the internet or method of storage is
      completely secure, so absolute security cannot be guaranteed.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">11. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on the hosting or service providers used, information may be processed or stored in countries outside
      your own. Where required, reasonable steps are taken to ensure appropriate safeguards are in place for such
      transfers.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">12. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-6 pb-0">12.1 GDPR / UK GDPR rights (where applicable)</h3>
    <p>
      Subject to applicable law, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to the
      processing of your personal data, and the right to data portability. You may also have the right to withdraw
      consent where processing is based on consent.
    </p>

    <p>
      To exercise these rights, please <SmartLink href="/contact/">contact</SmartLink>. A response will be provided
      within the timeframe required by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 pb-0">12.2 California privacy rights (CCPA/CPRA, where applicable)</h3>
    <p>
      If you are a California resident, you may have rights to know what personal information is collected, request
      deletion of personal information (subject to exceptions), and request correction of inaccurate personal
      information, among other rights under applicable California law.
    </p>

    <p>
      This Website does not sell personal information as those terms are generally understood under California privacy
      law.
    </p>

    <p>
      To make a privacy request, please <SmartLink href="/contact/">contact</SmartLink>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">13. Cookie Controls</h2>
    <p>
      You can manage cookies through your browser settings, including blocking or deleting cookies. If a cookie banner
      or consent tool is used on the Website, you may also manage preferences there.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">14. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This Website is not directed to children under 13, and personal information is not knowingly collected from
      children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the Website, please{" "}
      <SmartLink href="/contact/">contact</SmartLink>, and reasonable steps will be taken to delete that information.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">15. External Links</h2>
    <p>
      This Website may contain links to external websites (for example, GitHub, LinkedIn, or other third-party sites). I
      am not responsible for the content, security, or privacy practices of those external sites. Please review their
      privacy policies before providing personal information.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">16. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to reflect changes in the Website, legal requirements, or
      privacy practices. The updated version will be posted on this page with a revised “Last updated” date.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 pb-0">17. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions, concerns, or privacy requests, please use the contact form at{" "}
      <SmartLink href="/contact/">victor-fernandes.com/contact/</SmartLink>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
